From: Charles Pellegrini <c4ffein.work@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 15:54:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH v3 6/6] lib: scatterlist: add KUnit tests for sg_split()

Add a KUnit suite for lib/sg_split.c covering the (input shape, skip,
split sizes) matrix: full coverage, edge-aligned partial coverage,
mid-entry partial coverage at several boundary positions across one to
three input entries, skip-position variants, multi-split runs, zero-size
splits (including at the very end of the input), empty input entries,
and requests that must be rejected.

Each accepted case checks the documented post-conditions of sg_split():
the sum of each output split's entry lengths equals the requested split
size, and the bytes exposed by each split match the corresponding region
of the input. Backing memory uses a position-unique byte pattern so a
content mismatch pinpoints which input region was mis-exposed. It also
checks that every split is a list of at least one entry, end-marked on
its last entry only; that a zero-size split is exactly one entry of
length 0; and that a non-empty split does not start with a zero-length
entry. Each rejected case checks for -EINVAL and that out[] and
out_mapped_nents[] are left untouched.

Every case is run twice: unmapped (in_mapped_nents = 0, exercising
sg_split_phys()) and with an identity DMA mapping (dma_len == length,
contiguous synthetic IOVA, exercising sg_split_mapped() and asserting the
DMA addresses and lengths). A further group exercises divergent CPU/DMA
geometry (coalescing, where the DMA segmentation is coarser than the CPU
one), checking each split's CPU entry count and end marker and that it
has no more DMA entries than CPU entries; those cases need a distinct
dma_length field and are skipped where CONFIG_NEED_SG_DMA_LENGTH is not
selected.

Outputs are released through deferred KUnit actions, so a failed
assertion does not leak them.

With any one fix of this series reverted, the suite fails:

 - sg_calculate_split() overshoot: T5, T7, T9, T11, T13, T14 and T15
   (and D3 where it runs); T10 additionally guards the edge-aligned case
   that the 2021 fix proposal regressed;
 - sg_split_phys() ->length clobber (!NEED_SG_DMA_LENGTH builds only):
   the unmapped runs of T2, T3, T11, T12, T15 and T16;
 - splits starting at the end of the input: T8b, T8c and T8d;
 - zero-length first entry: T6, T13 and T17;
 - argument checks: T18.

Run with:

    tools/testing/kunit/kunit.py run sg_split

or, to also exercise the divergent cases and get precise reports for
out-of-bounds accesses:

    tools/testing/kunit/kunit.py run sg_split \
        --arch=x86_64 --kconfig_add=CONFIG_KASAN=y

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-4-8 hegel-c
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5 hegel-c
